      <h2>The Service</h2>
      <p>
        CircuitSimulate is a free, browser-based circuit simulator. It is provided at no cost and
        without a required account. We may change, add or remove features over time, and we may
        occasionally have to interrupt availability for maintenance or for reasons outside our
        control.
      </p>

      <h2>Simulation is a model, not reality</h2>
      <p>
        This is the most important thing to understand. CircuitSimulate is a tool for
        <strong>education and design exploration</strong>. Its results come from a numerical model
        of idealised components and are subject to modelling assumptions, simplifications and
        numerical limits.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>A working simulation is <strong>not</strong> a guarantee that a physical circuit will behave the same way.</li>
        <li>Do <strong>not</strong> rely on it for safety-critical, medical, or life-supporting decisions.</li>
        <li>Always validate a design with real measurement and sound engineering judgement before building, powering or shipping hardware.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You are responsible for how you interpret and apply the results.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You agree not to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Use the Service to break the law or to infringe someone else's rights.</li>
        <li>Attempt to disrupt, overload or compromise the Service or the infrastructure it runs on.</li>
        <li>Reverse the Service's protections in order to abuse it, or use it to distribute malware.</li>
        <li>Misrepresent the Service's output as a certified or validated engineering analysis.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your content</h2>
      <p>
        The circuits and projects you create are <strong>yours</strong>. They are stored locally in
        your browser and we do not claim ownership of them. Because your work stays on your device
        (see the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>), keeping backups — for example by exporting
        to <code>JSON</code> — is your responsibility.
      </p>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The Service itself — its software, design, branding and content that we author — is owned by
        CircuitSimulate and protected by applicable law. These terms do not transfer any of those
